# opp: the general principle (S2–S17) is drawn mainly from comparatives (greater/less, weaker/stronger), while life/death are contrary states. But S3 and S19 already count non-comparatives like good/evil and sleep/waking as opposites, so the text treats "opposite" in one sense throughout.
# gen: "generated out of" in S36 and S38 means the same thing in both directions (one state passing into the other); unsure only whether "the dead" shifts between dead bodies and souls of the dead, which the text does not mark.
